From 22ab8642d6f6f547a3d638e1d78805aa7ec3b4fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwen38-4090 <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:10:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/49] Low-bit screen for the DFlash2 proposal head with exact
 Q4 rescoring (NINFER_PROPOSAL_SCREEN, research25)

NINFER_PROPOSAL_SCREEN=3 (or 2) builds, at load, the half-offset G64 screen of screen_lowbit.cuh from the 131072-row Q4
G64 proposal head (3.25 bits per weight, 260 MiB) and runs the head's top-16 through it: screen, chunk merge, then an
exact FP32 rescoring of each column's top-R screen rows on the Q4 codes (NINFER_PROPOSAL_SCREEN_R = 32, 64, 128, 256;
R > 32 splits the rescoring across R/32 CTAs per column) and the top-16 keys in linear_topk's order. The candidate
selector normalizes over a column's 16 candidates only, so the drafts change only where an exact top-16 row falls
outside the screen's top-R. NINFER_PROPOSAL_SCREEN_CHECK=1 keeps the K-split drafts and prints the screen's recall.
screen_lowbit.cuh's non-template kernels get internal linkage (two screen TUs under -rdc).

Spec-Bench-480 forced on identical text (e2e31-dq3, research23 env), A B C A B C: 3-bit R32 ms/round -0.60% / -0.42%,
tok/step +0.10% (ns), tok/s +0.70% / +0.53%; R64 -0.47% / -0.27%; null 0.00%. nsys per call: screen path 352 us
(screen 325, merges 11, rescoring 16) vs the K-split path 458 us. Check mode: 3-bit R32 recall 0.908 of the exact
top-16, top-1 0.9993; 2-bit R128 recall 0.853, top-1 0.987 (not used).
